{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/76983-your-characters-and-their-actions-during-revolutions-upheavals","id":76983,"title":"Your characters and their actions during revolutions/upheavals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-22T05:04:39-08:00","id":76983,"title":"Your characters and their actions during revolutions/upheavals","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\">I listened to a podcast about the French revolution and that made me think about how you guys have used revolutions and similar upheavals in your games. Have your characters used the situations in order to make their own power grabs? What kind of ideological stances have you characters had or professed to have? Did you lose Backgrounds when the revolution came?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1298-the-chronicler","name":"The Chronicler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T07:11:10-08:00","id":77043,"title":"","content":"I've played in a VtM game set in Argentina during the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revoluci%C3%B3n_Libertadora\" target=\"_blank\">coups d'\u00e9tat of 1955</a>, which in our game resulted in open conflict between opposing factions of Kindred in Buenos Aires. My character was a Toreador <i>ancilla</i> who took the chance to erode the Lasombra <i>antitribu </i>power base by targeting specific churches and politicians, since he had a personal grudge against the bloodline from times past. He was a supporter of the Radical Civil Union, which took a few blows during the events of the coup (and thus costed him Influence), but he was too consumed by vengeance to care about it. Most of the power grabs resulted in higher influence of the Ventrue and the alienation of the Brujah (one whom was another player's character).<br /> <br /> It was fun, though the downside of it was two players dropping the game citing ideological reasons. That's what happens when you used real life events in a chronicle, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:37:37-08:00","id":77323,"title":"","content":"There was a situation in my LARP a few years ago that has since become known as The Night of Four Princes. It started as a coup by a Lasombra Antitribu who killed the elder Brujah prince and walked into Elysium with his ashes in a bag and his war coterie behind him and declared himself Prince.<br /> <br /> My character was an independent Caitiff troubleshooter, currently under indentured servitude to the Brujah by order of the old prince. I was quickly whisked off by my master who took me into meetings while they organized the armed resistance to this Lasombra's practice. Now I had had several good dealings with this Lasombra in the past and respected him greatly, so I just sat there unnoticed, texting him all the details of the plans against him. No one thought to look twice at me, it was great. <br /> <br /> Then the best part hit. I was an Obfuscate master, so they decided to have me Obfuscate their troops as they waited for the new Prince to show up, completely forgetting the fact that I was their prisoner and hated all of them. I quietly informed the new Prince of their positions and said for him to give me the signal when to drop the Obfuscate. When he showed up (he was Summoned) he gave the signal and their ambush utterly fell apart while I booked it out the back door. The Lasombra ended up getting killed anyway, as did a third declared Prince that night (hence Night of Four Princes) but it was still an amazing bit of treason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T00:57:11-08:00","id":80100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/76983-your-characters-and-their-actions-during-revolutions-upheavals?p=77323#post77323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a situation in my LARP a few years ago that has since become known as The Night of Four Princes. It started as a coup by a Lasombra Antitribu who killed the elder Brujah prince and walked into Elysium with his ashes in a bag and his war coterie behind him and declared himself Prince.<br /> <br /> My character was an independent Caitiff troubleshooter, currently under indentured servitude to the Brujah by order of the old prince. I was quickly whisked off by my master who took me into meetings while they organized the armed resistance to this Lasombra's practice. Now I had had several good dealings with this Lasombra in the past and respected him greatly, so I just sat there unnoticed, texting him all the details of the plans against him. No one thought to look twice at me, it was great.<br /> <br /> Then the best part hit. I was an Obfuscate master, so they decided to have me Obfuscate their troops as they waited for the new Prince to show up, <b>completely forgetting the fact that I was their prisoner and hated all of them. </b>I quietly informed the new Prince of their positions and said for him to give me the signal when to drop the Obfuscate. When he showed up (he was Summoned) he gave the signal and their ambush utterly fell apart while I booked it out the back door. The Lasombra ended up getting killed anyway, as did a third declared Prince that night (hence Night of Four Princes) but it was still an amazing bit of treason.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did they forget something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T08:55:59-08:00","id":80273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/76983-your-characters-and-their-actions-during-revolutions-upheavals?p=80100#post80100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did they forget something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being preoccupied or never really getting this character wasn't associating with them of his own free will. Easier for this to happen in Larp than in TT because PCs tend not to telegraph their opinions as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:52:40-08:00","id":80618,"title":"","content":"The best Changeling: the Dreaming campaign I ever ran was intended to be set during the Resurgence, with a motley of commoner PCs acting as specialists in Trod-Sabotage for the resistance forces. The first session, they screwed up thoroughly, got themselves captured by Sidhe knights, and executed. Instead of ending the campaign, I decided to use that as a prelude and improvised some stuff where they found each other in their next incarnations years later, now in a region of Concordia that was an especially dense Sidhe stronghold, in the early '80s (because I was still in the mood for a retro setting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:16:49-08:00","id":80637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How did they forget something like that? </div> </div> </div>These guys also were really not the brightest bunch to begin with. One of them tried to threaten me into raising my Humanity by saying if I didn't he'd punch me in the face. Yeah, that's going to make a Humanity 3 deranged sociopath more moral...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T19:24:56-08:00","id":81365,"title":"","content":"Well in my last game the city was being hit by a Sabbat death squad. My Nos was more concerned with staying alive then advancing in status. My biggest achievement of survival was hiding in a bar's septic tank to survive a missile strike. After that I was pretty safe by making myself useful by helping the prince's ghoul's to get communication back up and running. That is until we had to take on a demon. Again I mostly stayed out of the combat but had to dive out of the building via window when the demon exploded upon it's death taking my S.W.A.T. Armor with him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}